From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:17:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: usbdp: Re-enable DP lanes after a re-init with
 DP powered on

rk_udphy_init() programs the lane mux with all DP lanes disabled; they
are only enabled in rk_udphy_dp_phy_power_on(). When the Type-C mux
changes the configuration while the DP PHY is powered on, for example
when the DisplayPort Alt Mode pin assignment is changed from D to C or
back, rk_udphy_update_power_state() re-initializes the PHY but leaves
the DP lanes disabled. The DP controller then cannot retrain the link
(clock recovery fails on every lane) until DP is powered off and on
again by a full modeset.

Re-apply the DP bus width, lane enables and lane selection for the new
configuration after a re-init when DP is in use.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
index b0b777cca..4c90ddccd 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
@@ -1106,6 +1106,19 @@ static int rk_udphy_update_power_state(struct rk_udphy *udphy)
 			rk_udphy_run_reset_handler(udphy, false);
 			return ret;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * rk_udphy_init() leaves all DP lanes disabled. If the DP PHY
+		 * is powered on (the Type-C mux changed the pin assignment
+		 * while DP is in use), enable the lanes of the new
+		 * configuration again, as rk_udphy_dp_phy_power_on() does, so
+		 * that the DP controller can retrain the link.
+		 */
+		if ((udphy->sw_mode & UDPHY_MODE_DP) && (target_mode & UDPHY_MODE_DP)) {
+			phy_set_bus_width(udphy->phy_dp, udphy->dp_lanes);
+			rk_udphy_dp_lane_enable(udphy, udphy->dp_lanes);
+			rk_udphy_dp_lane_select(udphy);
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Ensure USB3 support is enabled when supported */
